  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Uganda SRL and other Countries to Improve TB Diagnosis in the ECSA Region - Africa - Multicountry Africa ECSA-HC (01-Jul-2019-30-Jun-2022)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry Africa ECSA-HC, Tuberculosis, East, Central and Southern Africa Health Community (ECSA-HC)This program has the following goals: Improving quality and diagnostic capacity of NRLs as well as build capacity to support TB Lab Networks in their countries. The objectives of this program are: Strengthening inter state regional network of national TB reference Laboratories (NRLs) for improved TB management in the ECSA region.  Improve Laboratory service provision for quality assurance, Phynotipic 1st and 2nd line DST.  Enhance impact of WHO Recommended Diagnositcs (WRD) in the region.  Consolidate capacity of NRLs to undertake epidemiological/national level disease monitoring surveys such as DRS, TB Prevalence and other Operational Research</narrative>
  </description>
